Expected elements: present

Every must-show item is on the page and no must-not-show item is. The surface reads as the desktop app: dark, dense, four panes, no explorer chrome.

Iteration changes. (1) Landed — the provenance sentences span the pane and set flush-left at x≈1157 under the `DATA`/badge row. (4) Landed — line 29 carries a dim `⊘`, line 32 a cyan `⊙`. (5) Landed in the identity bar (`← demo`, x≈22–75). (2) Not assessable: only `COST · MANA` (y≈762) is above the fold at 1440×900; `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` is below it. (3) Not present in view.

Confirmed at this viewport: the raw enum `Status reason: private-part-succeeded-public-part-succeeded` (tx pane, y≈188–210); the lowercase-slug opening of the EXECUTIONS sentence (y≈853); `mana (FeeJuice)` in the unit slot (y≈783). The terminal-full-stop question is unverifiable — the sentence is cut by the viewport edge.

Change (5) caused a new fault: the identity bar and badge now say `demo` while the EXECUTIONS prose still says `aztec`, so one page names two chains. Change (1) relocated the band's cost rather than removing it — the paragraph runs y≈228–450, about a quarter of the viewport, set larger and looser than every other row in a 292px pane, and pushes COST and EXECUTIONS to the fold. It is not too quiet; it is too loud here.

Highest-priority fixes: humanise the status reason, and reconcile `aztec`/`demo`.

Rating: 7/10

